e connects the serial transceiver line to +3V3.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The specified serial-mode jumpers should connect the two servo signal pins to the shared MAX3485 bus without tying that bus to a supply rail.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"source\": \"netlist\",\n          \"quote\": \"(net (name \\\"+3V3\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"R13\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\")))\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"netlist\",\n          \"quote\": \"(net (name \\\"Net-(J8-Pin_3)\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"R13\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\")) (node (ref \\\"R14\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\")))\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"netlist\",\n          \"quote\": \"(net (name \\\"/TTL\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"R14\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\")) ... (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A\\\")))\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"spec\",\n          \"quote\": \"Serial mode (populate R13/R14 ...): J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 are tied together into one shared bus node and driven by U1 (MAX3485)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"In the documented serial configuration, the MAX3485 bus is clamped to +3V3. The transceiver may be unable to transmit correctly and can be damaged when its output attempts to drive the line low.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.99\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist ties the first servo signal pin directly to +3V3 instead of routing PWM1 to it. It also makes the documented R13/R14 serial-jumper configuration connect the MAX3485 bus to +3V3.\"\n}",
